// holds because: AbstractLeastSquaresOptimizer#getChiSquare is documented as a Chi-Square-like value where the variances are the reciprocal of the weights; therefore after a successful optimize call it must equal the sum over measurements of weight[i] * residual[i]^2.
// valid input: Build a valid overdetermined least-squares problem through the real optimize API: a differentiable function f(x) = [x0, x0] with constant 2x1 Jacobian [[1],[1]], two distinct target values so the optimum has nonzero residuals, strictly positive weights, and any 1D start point.
