                "[oracle:probability-p] invariant violation: regularizedGammaP must be in [0,1]"
                    + " for valid inputs, but a=" + a + " x=" + x + " p=" + p);
        }
        if (!(q >= 0.0 && q <= 1.0)) {
            throw new FuzzerSecurityIssueLow(
                "[oracle:probability-q] invariant violation: regularizedGammaQ must be in [0,1]"
                    + " for valid inputs, but a=" + a + " x=" + x + " q=" + q);
        }
    }

    private static void driveRegularizedGammaQContinuedFractionPath(FuzzedDataProvider data) {
        /* Coverage-spread oracle for a different reachable function in the same region:
         * choose a >= 1 and x >= a so regularizedGammaQ takes its continued-fraction branch,
         * reaching ContinuedFraction.evaluate/getA/getB/logGamma through real library code.
         * For every correct implementation, P(a,x) + Q(a,x) = 1 still holds.
         */
